WEBVTT

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.630
Wein, wake up. It's morning.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.390
So soft.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.850
I wonder if he's dreaming.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.060
Maybe about me?

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.230
Her boobs are so big.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.190
And so soft, too.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.990
Wake the hell up, now!

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:21.410
Huh?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.000
If only our army hadn't
attacked with such gusto.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.470
That's what I'd hoped.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.470
But they took the gold mine
before I could stop them.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:08.100
But what's done is done.
Let's get as much out of it as we can.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.350
You sure?

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.980
That means...

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.400
Another battle with
Marden is all but certain.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.070
Pardon me.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:19.490
"Commander Larkurum, Kingdom of Natra"

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.530
"Commander Larkurum, Kingdom of Natra"
I've brought the man you wished to see.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.200
Perint. You're in charge of the miners.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.370
It is an honor to meet you, Your Highness.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.710
I've brought these documents for you.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.340
Let's see here.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.470
Perint, is this information to be trusted?

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.550
It is.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.680
In other words, the Jilaat Gold Mine is...

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.190
It's nearly spent.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.730
Y-You don't say?

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.150
What's the meaning of this?!

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:07.490
"King Fuschtarre, Kingdom of Marden"
Those lowly Natran maggots
have stolen the Jilaat Gold Mine?!

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.160
You are quite right to be angry, sire.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.080
We must respond to this outrage at once.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.250
"Finance Minister Holonuie,
Kingdom of Marden"
We must respond to this outrage at once.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:19.000
"Finance Minister Holonuie,
Kingdom of Marden"
Our loss in the Polta Wasteland left
the Jilaat Gold Mine ripe for the taking.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.760
Our loss in the Polta Wasteland left
the Jilaat Gold Mine ripe for the taking.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:26.090
As such, we should leave our forces
in the command of General Drawood.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:28.720
Thirty thousand troops should suffice.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.310
Hold on, Holonuie!

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.270
"Foreign Minister Midan,
Kingdom of Marden"
Moving that many troops
will leave our borders exposed!

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.190
We'll retake the mine

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.730
before the neighboring kingdoms
can muster their armies.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:44.820
I estimate it should
take no more than a week.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:51.450
Stop feeling sorry for yourself
and get back on your feet.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.250
Yeah, but...

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:59.250
We just fought Marden to get a
mine that ended up being worthless.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.920
How could I not be bummed out?

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.340
You can't sit around here doing nothing.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.680
You must set your policy moving forward.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.550
Policy? All we can do is withdraw.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.470
That's the least painful option.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:15.390
All right, shall we prepare
for an immediate withdrawal?

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.690
No.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.770
Abandoning the mine so soon
and in such a one-sided manner

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:24.820
puts the honor of our military
and the entire kingdom on the line.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.030
Wait! If we can reach
a stalemate with Marden,

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:33.700
maybe we could sue for peace
and have them buy back their mine.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.580
Perint says that Holonuie,
the official in charge of the mine,

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.170
doesn't know it is spent.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:44.760
That means no one else in
Marden likely knows, either.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.930
So you'll keep quiet about
the fact that it's worthless.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.760
The cost of this conquest keeps mounting.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.350
If there's money to be wrung
out of this, I'm gonna wring away!

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.690
Okay, fine. In that case,

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.690
we must quickly prepare to defend the mine

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.730
and keep a close eye on
Marden's movements, correct?

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:09.200
Marden will likely come
at us with a massive force.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.800
Marden's host numbers 30,000

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.050
against our 5,000.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.060
As you foresaw, Highness,
they threaten us with a mighty host.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.600
We should pull out if we can.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.650
If we don't, their superior numbers will
allow them to retake the mine in no time.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:48.530
They can't maintain
30,000 troops for very long.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.740
One month at most, I imagine.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.830
If we can hold out
and force them to withdraw,

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.370
our army can keep its honor intact,

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:01.880
and Marden will realize how difficult it
is to retake the mine by force.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.880
That will be our chance
to reach a peace agreement!

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.550
They've holed up instead of fleeing
before our superior force?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.260
"Commander Angrill, Kingdom of Marden"

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.600
"Commander Angrill, Kingdom of Marden"
A most foolish decision.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:13.930
I doubt those Natran barbarians
think as we do.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:17.850
"General Drawood, Kingdom of Marden"
I doubt those Natran barbarians
think as we do.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.930
Still, proceed with caution.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:23.440
We mustn't make a
tactical blunder like Urgio did.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.190
How can you say that, General Drawood?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.740
Our tactical skill is
beyond compare to Urgio's.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.150
And that's putting it lightly.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:37.540
It would be a shame if the enemy believed
that was the best Marden could do.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.410
Don't say that, Angrill.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.000
Even if it's true?

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.380
It's time, men.

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:48.300
Our month-long quagmire begins this day!

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.510
Halt Marden's advance!

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.850
Sweep them off the path!

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:06.270
It won't be long till we've taken
the mountain's third station.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.110
How can this be?!

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.860
How can Natra yet hold the advantage?!

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:17.200
Now then, what is your answer,
Princess Falanya?

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:17.700
"Gladius, Royal Tutor"

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:21.250
"Gladius, Royal Tutor"
So, in the battle at hand,

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:26.000
you're asking what the
most important consideration is?

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.170
Well...

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.960
Terrain! It's the terrain, isn't it?!

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.380
Indeed it is.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.470
The paths up the mountain
are not very wide.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:39.350
It would be impossible
to array 30,000 troops there.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:40.600
As such,

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:46.310
only several hundred each of our 5,000
and their 30,000 can clash at a time.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:50.980
But it's a gold mine.
Can't it be attacked from behind?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.320
Knowing Prince Wein,

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.910
he has likely whittled away
at the mountainside

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.240
to keep the enemy from climbing up!

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.620
Can't they build a new path up?

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:07.500
There are already three frontal paths up
to Natra's stronghold at the summit.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.290
--As such--
--I know!

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:11.630
Marden is reluctant to build new paths up.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:15.680
We want them to think taking
the mine by force is the easiest way!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.430
Precisely. And...

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:22.640
My strategy rests on
making them believe that.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:25.940
So, what will it be, Drawood?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:31.820
Whatever action you take,
I'll have you in the palm of my hand.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.070
"Third Day of Battle"
It's 30,000 against 5,000!

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:39.320
Why can't you take that mountain
despite their meager numbers?!

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.030
Those damn barbarians!

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:42.370
Excuse me, sir!

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.710
I have an important report
from our scouts!

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:51.920
They discovered an old mine shaft leading
to the heart of the Natran camp.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.300
What?

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.220
Okay, here's what we do...

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:03.060
We'll catch those beasts unawares!

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.480
Light the torches!

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.780
It's a trap! Retreat!

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.740
After them! Don't let any escape!

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.370
It's just like General Drawood said!

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.870
They can use this mine shaft
to escape in a pinch

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:28.420
and secretly dispatch soldiers
to ambush our forces.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:32.340
They must've left it open as a trump card.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:37.920
But they have yet to learn
that we've discovered it.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:42.260
We need not fear the Natrans
once they lose their terrain advantage.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:45.310
Pierce their heart in one fell stroke!

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.730
It's hard to run in heavy armor.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.240
Huh?

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.450
They have no armor or weapons.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.540
Wait a second.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.290
Have we been lured into a trap?!

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.670
Well done.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.790
So that was your plan.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:18.510
You're trying to demoralize their general.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.390
I've no way to defeat an army
of 30,000 with 5,000 troops.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:26.060
But the commander behind that 30,000

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.770
is within my grasp.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.600
The more we wound Drawood's pride,
the more his judgment suffers,

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.270
and their tactical agility dulls.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:38.230
And that means the advantage
will fall in our favor.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.490
I already knew it, but you're
quite diabolical, aren't you?

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:46.620
Truth be told, I'm rather proud of that.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:49.910
Damn him to hell!

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.670
How dare that lowly cur

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.420
make such a fool of me!

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.750
G-General!

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.710
Losing Angrill is indeed a setback.

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:02.970
But they've lost their only escape route.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.800
That can be considered a win for us.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.850
You're right.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:13.690
Go ahead and celebrate, you barbarians.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.560
I will tear you limb from limb
before this is over!

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.150
"The Next Day"

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:28.160
The fort near the first station
has fallen to our forces!

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.830
They did it!

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:40.090
Okay, let's light 'em up!

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:40.960
Highness!

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:44.050
With me! Charge!

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.980
General! We're under attack!

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.480
General!

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:01.150
There are reports of Natran troops
setting our camps ablaze!

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:02.280
How many?!

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:06.110
They say no more than a hundred cavalry
or as many as several hundred.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:08.280
Where are they now?!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.910
We don't know that, either!

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.920
Wh-What the hell?!

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.130
Don't tell me they're storming down
with their entire army?!

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.710
This can't be!

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:25.510
We have 30,000! We can't be
vanquished by a force of 5,000!

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:30.640
No, they can't defeat our forces.
Maybe they're targeting my headquarters.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.890
They could be trying to storm
through our confused troops

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.980
and claim the heads of our commanders!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.730
It's entirely possible!

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:43.650
Have all troops nearby assemble and
form a defense line here at headquarters!

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.860
Have all the other camps standby!

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:47.610
Y-Yes, sir!

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.070
Do not underestimate me.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:53.580
You will not claim my head so easily!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.420
Boulders and logs?

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:06.420
Is that what we heard bearing down on us,
rather than Natran horsemen?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.800
But the question is why?

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.640
The first station fort!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:15.390
The Natran troops have reoccupied it!

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:21.310
Y-Y-You no-good scum!

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:24.940
"Two Weeks Later"

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.440
"Two Weeks Later"
Wow!

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.570
This is going way better than I planned!

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.320
Our food stores are adequate.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.490
Our other supplies are dwindling,
but there's enough for now.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:39.540
And thanks to our well-fought battles,
troop morale remains high.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:43.880
Meanwhile, Marden's offensive
has weakened considerably.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:46.260
I wonder if they'll withdraw.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.970
Ain't gonna happen.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:52.640
Their losses are now utterly unacceptable,
as they have nothing to show for them.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:57.560
But I expect to kiss this siege lifestyle
goodbye in a couple of weeks.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.690
That would be most welcome.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.400
I'm tired of the view from this mountain.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:07.030
And I could use a bath,
but hot water is a luxury up here.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:10.570
You did use to stand closer to me.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.370
You must stink--

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.990
Don't say such things.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.660
Don't think you've won this one!

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:19.750
This isn't about winning or losing.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.460
Pardon me, Your Highness.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.050
There's an envoy from Marden's army.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.880
An envoy?

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.590
In these negotiations,

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.090
"Army Commander Logan, Kingdom of Marden"
know that I speak for General Drawood.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.060
My words are his.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.020
Now then, Prince Wein,

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.980
your pet dogs that made
themselves at home here,

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.230
or should I say, your ability
to control them is impressive.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:49.530
General Drawood thinks highly of you.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.450
Commander Logan, may I ask
what brings you here today?

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:59.040
You haven't trekked all the way up
here to provoke us, have you?

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:03.460
I'm here for no other reason than
to forge a peace agreement.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:06.840
Let me state our terms.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.590
First, you must withdraw
from the mine at once,

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.880
surrender your weapons,
and free the mining town's residents.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.510
And then, of course,

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:20.100
we demand compensation for
your unjust occupation of our mine.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.730
That's quite an ask.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.100
What say you, Prince Wein?

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.610
That's no peace treaty.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:29.730
It's unconditional surrender.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:34.160
I'm afraid we can't
seek peace on those terms.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:38.870
I see. Well, it seems you really have
surrounded yourself with filthy mutts.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.790
Let me give you a bit of friendly advice.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:47.130
You should have someone by your side
who can question your folly.

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:50.840
In particular,

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:55.050
you should discard
that dirty Flahm at once.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:57.970
Keeping a servant of such
lowly birth by your side

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.930
is unbecoming of your noble lineage.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.740
Commander Logan.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:17.200
You told me that your words
are General Drawood's.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.410
Is that true?

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.160
Yes, but what of it?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.870
Never mind.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:29.750
Tell the good general
I wish him all the best.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:35.130
It's been three weeks since this began.

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.510
This disgrace ends here today.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:44.180
We will stain this mountain red
with barbarian blood before sundown.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:47.440
Our all-out offensive... begins now!

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.240
It's but a matter of time till they fall.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.780
General!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:03.700
Is General Drawood here?!

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.540
I have an urgent message
from Commander Logan!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.960
What is it?! Quickly now!

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.750
Yes, sir. Here it is.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.380
Logan!

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:17.550
See you in hell!

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:19.430
How dare you!

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:31.400
D-Don't tell me it's you?!

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:36.110
I don't believe we've met before,
General Drawood.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:38.570
Wein?! Why are you here?!

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:41.740
It's simple. I'm here for your head.

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:42.830
H-Help!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.290
No one's coming.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:49.120
Your men have their hands full,
trying to take back the mountain.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.670
They're not concerned
with your headquarters.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:55.380
They must have noticed you
people coming down the mountain.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.680
Once they report that
to one of their officers--

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:01.970
We didn't come down the mountain.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:05.060
You remember that mine shaft, don't you?

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.690
That deathtrap? It would take
months to clear the rubble.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.900
The one next to it.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:15.980
I had the miners dig a
parallel shaft well in advance.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:19.990
It connects from the mine's interior
all the way to the cave entrance.

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:21.240
Don't tell me...!

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.030
That's right. The shaft
collapse wasn't a trap.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.040
It was a way to make you
forget about the cave.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.960
All we had to do was dig
the final connecting shaft,

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.790
disguise ourselves with your armor,
and stroll on out.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:38.550
No one would ever
take us for Natran soldiers.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:43.220
So, you had me in the palm
of your hand the entire time.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:54.940
Truth be told, I hadn't planned on
joining this little jaunt.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:04.490
Ninym is my heart.

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:07.990
And all who wound my heart...

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:15.790
...shall die by my own hand.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.500
What?

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:22.130
Crown Prince Wein attended
the empire's military academy?!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:27.180
It can't be. I never saw any
mention of that in my research.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.600
That must be it.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.890
All these redacted top grades...

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:36.020
The empire hid the shameful fact
that a royal from another kingdom

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:40.190
bested their imperial cadets in every way.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:42.240
This can't be happening.

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:47.080
We, the empire, are responsible
for letting the fangs grow,

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.700
the fangs that will sink into our necks.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:55.380
Wein Salema Arbalest,
you are a terrifying man, indeed.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.750
Now, I raise my glass to Natra's victory!

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.300
--To Natra!
--To Natra!

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:06.640
The prince regent is a marvel indeed.
What a magnificent victory.

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:10.220
I wish you could have seen
Prince Wein's heroic actions!

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:13.230
He has a valiance that stirs the heart!

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.980
Your Highness.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:18.190
May I have a word?

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:24.030
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:28.660
We just received news from a spy
we have in Marden's capital.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:29.740
News?

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.700
Marden's capital has fallen.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.120
It's fallen?

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.080
Marden's Capital?! Who did this and how?!

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.960
Its neighbor, Cavarin.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.380
Many of the city's troops
were fighting us,

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.930
so it fell quickly
and with little resistance.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:49.180
King Fuschtarre perished,
and that's not all.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:50.810
Ninym.

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:55.560
I was supposed to be attending peace
negotiations with Marden after this.

00:21:55.560 --> 00:22:00.360
Yes, but the kingdom you sought
to make peace with has fallen.

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:03.400
Our hopes have gone up in smoke.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:07.700
I didn't even have time to sell that mine!

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:10.910
I also have a report from Perint.

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:13.580
Huh? "We have found a new gold vein."

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:14.910
What?! Seriously?!

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:16.160
So it seems.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:20.540
It's no return to the glory days,
but it will get us out of the red.

00:22:22.170 --> 00:22:26.340
I was dreading telling the military
that the mine was worthless,

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:29.760
but it seems I was saved by the bell!

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:33.850
All right! This has bought me some time!

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:35.980
I've been so busy since we returned.

00:22:35.980 --> 00:22:37.810
Now I can take some time off--

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:39.190
No!

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:44.650
Ambassadors from nations in
the west wish to meet with you.

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:47.740
Our officials need to speak
to you about budgetary matters.

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:50.570
Also, Princess Falanya misses you,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:54.330
and you have town inspections
that were postponed during the war.

00:22:54.330 --> 00:22:57.910
There's still so much left to do.

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:06.260
I can't wait to sell
this kingdom and disappear!
